From: pleft <elefasgr@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 18:11:20 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 14/16] PSP2DC: the companion's Maple command and its two byte
 queues (protocol 7)

A Dreamcast program sends command 0x50 to the memory card unit; the adapter
answers at once from two queues in RAM, one towards the PSP and one towards
the Dreamcast, or "again" when a SEND has no room yet. The USB driver moves
the bytes: COMP_DATA after whatever else a transfer carries (a transfer is
now up to 1280 bytes), COMP_EVENT from the PSP, COMP_RESET when a session
begins. Status carries the companion's counts.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
